      "text" : "Play D3 and win South's ace, retaining DK. Develop clubs by cashing CA and CK, following with dummy's small clubs, then leading a low club to CQ. A 3–2 break supplies five clubs: cash HK, cross to HA and cash South's winners for ten tricks. Against a 4–1 break, after CQ lead a LOW heart to HA, preserving HK, then concede the fourth club to establish South's fifth. Keep DK, SA and HK intact until that concession: each side suit remains stopped. Win a heart return with HK and return to South through diamonds to DK or spades to SA; on a diamond or spade return, win in South, cash the established club and arrange to collect HK before using the other South entry. Four clubs, two diamonds, two hearts and SA yield nine tricks. Do not cash both heart honors before surrendering the club. If clubs prove 5–0 on the first round, reconsider the club sequence using the revealed position and spot cards; four club tricks and the contract are no longer assured.",
